@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `usca-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `usca-holidays`

-- California days the Governor is directed to proclaim: Gov. Code §§ 6708-6729, 6731, 6733, 6735 and 6736.
--
-- Added in pass 2 of the completion to "whole".  Pass 1 called these 26 sections "not applicable" because they proclaim commemorative days and do not
-- add to the list of holidays of Gov. Code § 6700(a); the brief has no such disposition, and a section that tells an official to proclaim a day is encoded
-- as what it means for the individual: which day, in which year, whether the duty recurs, and what a proclamation does not do.
-- The quotation lines are copied by script from the converter-made plain-text rendering of the sections (not the official text) and checked against it by
-- srcrefs.py.  Target: unstable (REFUSE).  Imports: prelude, daydate, usca-interpretation-time (for `Moment`) and usca-holidays (for the n-th weekday of a month).
--
-- Fork F-hol-6: whether a day the Governor proclaims is a holiday.  None of these sections calls its day a holiday, and Gov. Code § 6700(a)(20)(A) makes holidays of
-- "every day appointed by the President or Governor for a public fast, thanksgiving, or holiday"; the text does not say whether a commemorative proclamation is such an
-- appointment.  The answer is a named refusal, and a caller who treats a proclamation as an appointment supplies the day to usca-holidays.l4.
-- Fork F-proclaim-once: Gov. Code §§ 6708-6711 say the Governor "shall proclaim" a day "to be known hereafter" and do not say "annually"; the others do.

§ `The days the Governor is directed to proclaim: Gov. Code §§ 6708-6736`

DECLARE `Way of fixing the day` IS ONE OF
    `a fixed date`
    `an ordinal weekday of a month`
    `a whole month`
    `the days of remembrance around a fixed date`
    `the astronomical Northward equinox`

DECLARE `Whether the duty recurs` IS ONE OF
    `the text says the duty recurs each year`
    `the text does not say whether the duty recurs`

-- The fields, in order: the section, the name the day is to be known by, the way the section fixes the day, the month, the day of the month or which weekday of the
-- month (the 3rd Saturday: 3), the weekday (0 Sunday ... 6 Saturday, as in daydate; 0 when the day is not fixed by a weekday), and whether the duty recurs.
DECLARE Proclamation HAS
    section                         IS A STRING
    `name`                          IS A STRING
    `how the day is fixed`          IS A `Way of fixing the day`
    `month`                         IS A NUMBER
    `day of the month or which one` IS A NUMBER
    `weekday`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the duty`                      IS A `Whether the duty recurs`

DECLARE `Period of days` HAS
    `first day` IS A DATE
    `last day`  IS A DATE

