GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date with year, month and day` y m d MEANS
    YMD y m d

-- The Sunday strictly before a date that is not a Sunday, and the Sunday strictly after it (weekday 0 is Sunday, as in daydate).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Sunday before the date` d MEANS
    d MINUS `Weekday of` d

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Sunday after the date` d MEANS
    d PLUS (7 MINUS `Weekday of` d)

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A Proclamation
`the proclamation under` s MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's section EQUALS s) `the proclamations of Gov. Code §§ 6708-6736`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN REFUSE "the number is not a section of Gov. Code §§ 6708-6736 in the deposited text (6730, 6732 and 6734 are absent from it)"
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN p

-- The days a proclamation under the section directs, in a year.  A whole month is the period from its first day to its last; the days of remembrance
-- of § 6720 run "from the Sunday before that day through the following Sunday", read as the Sunday strictly before and strictly after April 24; in a year when
-- April 24 is itself a Sunday the text does not say which Sunday is meant, and the function refuses (fork F-6720).
-- The equinox of § 6727 is an astronomical fact the text does not compute: it is an input.
GIVEN s IS A STRING
      year IS A NUMBER
      equinox IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`the days the Governor is directed to proclaim under` s `in the year` year `given the day of the astronomical Northward equinox:` equinox MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF p's `how the day is fixed` EQUALS `a fixed date`
            THEN `Period of days` OF fixedDay, fixedDay
        IF p's `how the day is fixed` EQUALS `an ordinal weekday of a month`
            THEN `Period of days` OF ordinalDay, ordinalDay
        IF p's `how the day is fixed` EQUALS `a whole month`
            THEN `Period of days` OF (`the date with year, month and day` year m 1), (`the date with year, month and day` year m (`Days in month` m year))
        IF p's `how the day is fixed` EQUALS `the days of remembrance around a fixed date` AND `Weekday of` fixedDay EQUALS 0
            THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code § 6720 runs the days of remembrance from the Sunday before April 24 through the following Sunday; when April 24 is itself a Sunday the text does not say whether that day is the Sunday meant"
        IF p's `how the day is fixed` EQUALS `the days of remembrance around a fixed date`
            THEN `Period of days` OF (`the Sunday before the date` fixedDay), (`the Sunday after the date` fixedDay)
        IF isNothing equinox
            THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code § 6727 names the day of the astronomical Northward equinox, which the text does not compute; the day is an input"
        OTHERWISE `Period of days` OF equinoxDay, equinoxDay
    WHERE
        p MEANS `the proclamation under` s
        m MEANS p's month
        n MEANS p's `day of the month or which one`
        wd MEANS p's weekday
        fixedDay MEANS `the date with year, month and day` year m n
        ordinalDay MEANS `the n-th given weekday of a month` n wd m year
        equinoxDay MEANS fromMaybe fixedDay equinox

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section directs a proclamation every year` s MEANS
    CONSIDER (`the proclamation under` s)'s `the duty`
    WHEN `the text says the duty recurs each year` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the text does not say whether the duty recurs` THEN REFUSE "this section says the Governor shall proclaim the day to be known hereafter by its name, and does not say annually; the text does not say whether the duty recurs each year"

-- Fork F-hol-6.
GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a proclamation under the section makes the day a holiday` s MEANS
    REFUSE "no section of Gov. Code §§ 6708-6736 calls its day a holiday; whether a day the Governor proclaims is a day appointed for a public fast, thanksgiving, or holiday under Gov. Code § 6700(a)(20)(A) is not said"

§ `Gov. Code § 6726: Space Day`

-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:96 | 6726. (a) The Governor shall proclaim the first Friday in May of each year to be Space Day and designate that date as having special significance in public schools and educational institutions. The Governor shall encourage public schools and educational institutions to conduct suitable commemorative exercises on that date.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:97 | (b) The Governor shall encourage every resident, business, and public entity to dim or turn off their lights between 9 p.m. and 10
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:98 | p.m. on Space Day.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:99 | (c) Space Day shall promote space observation and appreciation, promote California’s aerospace industry, and encourage students to pursue careers in science, technology, engineering, and mathematics.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:100 | (d) The Governor shall direct the Department of General Services to turn off the nonessential lights on the State Capitol Building between 9:00 p.m. and 10:00 p.m. on Space Day as a symbolic act designed to encourage all California citizens, businesses, and other entities to voluntarily dim or turn off their lights on Space Day.
-- (a) designates the date as having special significance in public schools and educational institutions, and tells the Governor to encourage them to conduct commemorative
-- exercises; (b) tells the Governor to encourage every resident, business and public entity to dim or turn off their lights between 9 p.m. and 10 p.m.; (d) tells the Governor to
-- direct the Department of General Services to turn off the nonessential lights on the State Capitol Building in that hour, "as a symbolic act designed to encourage ... to
-- voluntarily dim or turn off their lights".  The Governor is the one under a duty; the text asks nothing of a school, a resident, a business or a public entity.
@ref Gov. Code § 6726(a), (b), (d) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:96-100)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a school, educational institution, resident, business or public entity is required to take part in Space Day` MEANS
    FALSE

DECLARE `Kind of light on the State Capitol Building` IS ONE OF
    `a nonessential light`
    `an essential light`

@ref Gov. Code § 6726(d) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:100)
GIVEN light IS A `Kind of light on the State Capitol Building`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Governor is to direct the Department of General Services to turn off the light on Space Day` light MEANS
    CONSIDER light
    WHEN `a nonessential light` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an essential light` THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code § 6726(d) directs the nonessential lights to be turned off; it does not say that an essential light is to stay on"

-- Fork F-between: "between 9 p.m. and 10 p.m.": the instants 9 p.m. and 10 p.m. themselves are not said to be inside (as for the instant of sunrise in Gov. Code § 6807).
@ref Gov. Code § 6726(b), (d) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:97-100)
GIVEN moment IS A Moment
      theYear IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the moment falls in the lights-out hour of Space Day` moment `of the year` theYear MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (moment's `the day` EQUALS spaceDay)
            THEN FALSE
        IF moment's `seconds after midnight` EQUALS 21 TIMES 3600 OR moment's `seconds after midnight` EQUALS 22 TIMES 3600
            THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code § 6726 says between 9 p.m. and 10 p.m.; it does not say whether the instant of 9 p.m. or of 10 p.m. is inside"
        OTHERWISE moment's `seconds after midnight` GREATER THAN 21 TIMES 3600 AND moment's `seconds after midnight` LESS THAN 22 TIMES 3600
    WHERE
        spaceDay MEANS `the n-th given weekday of a month` 1 5 5 theYear
